<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.4.4: Finding the Solution to an Equation in One Variable, Part 2</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00116</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.4.4: Finding the Solution to an Equation in One Variable, Part 2</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d70803d7-56e2-489a-b009-52ab91228248</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">An empty shipping box weighs 250 grams. The box is then filled with T-shirts. Each T-shirt weighs 132.5 grams.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">The equation \( W = 250 + 132.5T \) represents the relationship between the quantities in this situation, where \( W \) is the weight, in grams, of the filled box and \( T \) is the number of shirts in the box.</para>
      <!--Q1 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Name two possible solutions to the equation \( W = 250 + 132.5T \).</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Your answer may vary, but here are some examples:</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>\(T=2\) and \(W=515\) </item>
            <item>\(T=10\) and \(W=1575\) </item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q2 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">What do the solutions mean in this situation?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00008">Each solution tells us the number of T-shirts in the box and the corresponding total weight in grams.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3 -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">Consider the equation \( 2,\!900 = 250 + 132.50T \). In this situation, what does the solution to this equation tell us?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011">It tells us the number of T-shirts in the box that results in a total weight of 2,900 grams.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>